{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"servos","name":"More servos: 360, continuous, winch and smart","version":"1.0.1","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Servos beyond 180 degrees. Continuous ones that spin round and round (FS90R, MG996R 360: the signal sets speed and direction), positional ones with 270 and 360 degrees of travel, a sail winch servo that turns three and a half turns, and two smart serial-bus servos that turn to any angle and report back (Feetech STS3215 with SCServo.h, Dynamixel XL430 with Dynamixel2Arduino.h).","category":"Motion","needsApp":"0.4.3","code":"// Servos beyond 180 degrees. The PWM ones read the pulse width on SIG (io.pwm: duty / frequency);\r\n// the smart ones speak their real serial protocols on DATA.\r\n\r\n/** the pulse on a servo's signal wire, in microseconds (0: none) */\r\nconst pulseOf = (io) => {\r\n  const p = io.pwm('SIG');\r\n  if (!p || p.hz < 30 || p.hz > 400) return 0;\r\n  const us = (p.duty / p.hz) * 1e6;\r\n  return us >= 400 && us <= 2700 ? us : 0;\r\n};\r\nconst supplied = (io) => io.supply('V+', 'GND');\r\n\r\n// A continuous-rotation servo: the position sensor is gone, so the pulse sets SPEED: 1500 us (write(90))\r\n// stops it, 1000 / 2000 us are full speed each way. Real ones stop a little off 1500 (the trim).\r\nbench.device('cr-servo', (part) => {\r\n  const horn = part.motor('horn');\r\n  const trim = Number(part.params.trim ?? 0);\r\n  let us = 0, v = 0, power = 0;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      v = supplied(io);\r\n      us = pulseOf(io);\r\n      if (v < 3.5 || !us) { horn.power(0, 0); power = 0; io.draw(v >= 3.5 ? 0.006 : 0); return; }\r\n      const off = us - 1500 - trim;\r\n      power = Math.abs(off) < 25 ? 0 : Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, -off / 500)); // (25 us dead band)\r\n      horn.power(power, v);\r\n      io.draw(power ? 0.12 + 0.5 * Math.abs(power) * (horn.stalled ? 2 : 0.4) : 0.008);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (v < 3.5) return ['no power'];\r\n      if (!us) return ['no signal: stopped'];\r\n      return [`pulse ${Math.round(us)} us: ${power ? `${Math.round(Math.abs(power) * 100)} % ${power > 0 ? 'anticlockwise' : 'clockwise'}` : 'stopped'}`, `${Math.round(horn.speed / 6)} rpm`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// A positional servo with more travel: 500-2500 us spread over its whole range (270 or 360 deg).\r\nbench.device('pwm-servo', (part) => {\r\n  const horn = part.motor('horn');\r\n  const half = Number(part.params.range ?? 270) / 2;\r\n  let us = 0, v = 0, want = 0;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      v = supplied(io);\r\n      us = pulseOf(io);\r\n      if (v < 3.5 || !us) { horn.limp(); io.draw(v >= 3.5 ? 0.006 : 0); return; }\r\n      want = Math.max(-half, Math.min(half, ((us - 1500) / 1000) * half));\r\n      horn.to(want, v);\r\n      io.draw(Math.abs(horn.speed) > 5 || horn.stalled ? (horn.stalled ? 2.5 : 0.5) : 0.015);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (v < 3.5) return ['no power'];\r\n      if (!us) return ['no signal (limp)'];\r\n      return [`pulse ${Math.round(us)} us: to ${Math.round(want)} deg, at ${Math.round(horn.angle)} deg${horn.stalled ? ' (stalled)' : ''}`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// A sail winch servo: 600-2400 us over three and a half turns (-630 .. +630 deg), held there.\r\nbench.device('winch-servo', (part) => {\r\n  const horn = part.motor('horn');\r\n  let us = 0, v = 0, want = 0;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      v = supplied(io);\r\n      us = pulseOf(io);\r\n      if (v < 3.5 || !us) { horn.limp(); io.draw(v >= 3.5 ? 0.006 : 0); return; }\r\n      want = Math.max(-630, Math.min(630, ((us - 1500) / 900) * 630));\r\n      horn.to(want, v);\r\n      io.draw(Math.abs(horn.speed) > 5 || horn.stalled ? (horn.stalled ? 2.2 : 0.6) : 0.02);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (v < 3.5) return ['no power'];\r\n      if (!us) return ['no signal (limp)'];\r\n      return [`pulse ${Math.round(us)} us: to ${Math.round(want)} deg (${(want / 360).toFixed(2)} turns), at ${Math.round(horn.angle)} deg${horn.stalled ? ' (stalled)' : ''}`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- smart servos\r\n// Both keep a goal and move there at their speed; their horn is a multi-turn joint (any angle).\r\n// Position 2048 is the middle (where the horn starts): 4096 counts a turn.\r\nconst DEG = 360 / 4096;\r\n\r\n// Feetech STS3215 (the SCS/STS protocol): FF FF id len instr params checksum, at 1,000,000 baud.\r\n// Memory: 5 ID, 33 mode (0 position, 1 wheel), 40 torque on, 41 acceleration, 42 goal position,\r\n// 44 goal time, 46 goal speed, 56 present position, 58 present speed, 60 load, 62 voltage (0.1 V),\r\n// 63 temperature, 66 moving. 16-bit values low byte first; speeds and wheel speed: bit 15 = backwards.\r\nbench.device('sts-servo', (part) => {\r\n  const horn = part.motor('horn');\r\n  const mem = new Array(80).fill(0);\r\n  const id = () => mem[5];\r\n  mem[5] = Number(part.params.id ?? 1) & 0xff;\r\n  mem[3] = 9; mem[4] = 0; // model\r\n  mem[6] = 0; // baud: 1,000,000\r\n  mem[11] = 4095 & 255; mem[12] = 4095 >> 8; // max angle limit\r\n  mem[40] = 1; // torque on\r\n  mem[63] = 32;\r\n  mem[42] = 2048 & 255; mem[43] = 2048 >> 8; // (the goal starts where it is: the middle)\r\n  // (in position mode it counts within one turn, 0-4095: \"base\" is where that turn starts, in the\r\n  //  horn's own degrees; spinning as a wheel moves it on, and position mode picks up from that turn)\r\n  let rx = [], v = 0, goalDeg = 0, cmdDeg = 0, vel = 0, lastT = 0, got = 0, replies = [], baudOk = true, base = 0, lastMode = 0;\r\n  const w16 = (a) => mem[a] | (mem[a + 1] << 8);\r\n  const sgn = (x) => (x & 0x8000 ? -(x & 0x7fff) : x);\r\n  const set16 = (a, x) => { mem[a] = x & 255; mem[a + 1] = (x >> 8) & 255; };\r\n  const chk = (bytes) => ~bytes.reduce((s, b) => s + b, 0) & 0xff;\r\n  const reply = (err, params = []) => {\r\n    const body = [id(), params.length + 2, err, ...params];\r\n    replies.push([0xff, 0xff, ...body, chk(body)]);\r\n  };\r\n  const handle = (pkt) => {\r\n    const [tid, len, ins, ...rest] = pkt;\r\n    const params = rest.slice(0, len - 2);\r\n    got++;\r\n    const forMe = tid === id() || tid === 0xfe;\r\n    if (ins === 0x01) { if (tid === id()) reply(0); return; }\r\n    if (ins === 0x02 && tid === id()) { const [a, n] = params; reply(0, mem.slice(a, a + n)); return; }\r\n    if (ins === 0x03 && forMe) {\r\n      const a = params[0];\r\n      for (let i = 1; i < params.length; i++) if (a + i - 1 < 80 && a + i - 1 !== 56) mem[a + i - 1] = params[i] & 255;\r\n      if (tid === id()) reply(0);\r\n      return;\r\n    }\r\n    if (ins === 0x83) { // SYNC WRITE: addr, len per servo, then [id, data...] for each\r\n      const [a, n] = params;\r\n      for (let i = 2; i + n < params.length + 1; i += n + 1)\r\n        if (params[i] === id()) {\r\n          for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) mem[a + k] = params[i + 1 + k];\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n  return {\r\n    packets(list) {\r\n      for (const p of list) {\r\n        if (p.pin !== 'DATA' && p.pin !== 'DATA2') continue;\r\n        if (p.proto !== 'uart') continue;\r\n        baudOk = !p.baud || Math.abs(p.baud - 1000000) < 30000;\r\n        if (!baudOk) continue;\r\n        rx.push(...p.data);\r\n      }\r\n      // whole packets: FF FF id len ...\r\n      for (let guard = 0; guard < 64; guard++) { // (whole packets, a few at most)\r\n        const s = rx.findIndex((b, i) => b === 0xff && rx[i + 1] === 0xff && rx[i + 2] !== 0xff);\r\n        if (s < 0) { if (rx.length > 512) rx = []; break; }\r\n        if (rx.length < s + 4) break;\r\n        const len = rx[s + 3];\r\n        if (rx.length < s + 4 + len) break;\r\n        const pkt = rx.slice(s + 2, s + 4 + len);\r\n        rx = rx.slice(s + 4 + len);\r\n        if (chk(pkt.slice(0, -1)) === pkt[pkt.length - 1]) handle(pkt.slice(0, -1));\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      v = Math.max(supplied(io), io.supply('V+2', 'GND2'));\r\n      const dt = io.time - lastT;\r\n      lastT = io.time;\r\n      if (v < 4) { horn.limp(); rx = []; replies = []; io.draw(0); return; }\r\n      for (const r of replies) io.send('DATA', 'uart', r, 1000000);\r\n      replies = [];\r\n      const torque = mem[40] & 1;\r\n      const wheel = mem[33] === 1;\r\n      if (!wheel && lastMode === 1) base = 360 * Math.floor((horn.angle + 180) / 360); // (back to positions: within this turn)\r\n      lastMode = mem[33];\r\n      goalDeg = base + (sgn(w16(42)) - 2048) * DEG;\r\n      const top = 45 * 6 * (v / 7.4); // deg/s at this voltage\r\n      const spd = Math.min(top, (sgn(w16(46)) ? Math.abs(sgn(w16(46))) * DEG : top) || top);\r\n      const acc = mem[41] ? mem[41] * 100 * DEG : 1e9; // (deg/s^2: 100 counts/s^2 a step of ACC)\r\n      if (wheel) {\r\n        const want = Math.max(-top, Math.min(top, sgn(w16(46)) * DEG));\r\n        vel += Math.max(-acc * dt, Math.min(acc * dt, want - vel));\r\n        cmdDeg += vel * dt;\r\n      } else {\r\n        const d = goalDeg - cmdDeg;\r\n        const stop = Math.sqrt(2 * acc * Math.abs(d));\r\n        const wantV = Math.sign(d) * Math.min(spd, stop);\r\n        vel += Math.max(-acc * dt, Math.min(acc * dt, wantV - vel));\r\n        if (Math.abs(d) < Math.abs(vel * dt) || Math.abs(d) < 0.05) { cmdDeg = goalDeg; vel = 0; } else cmdDeg += vel * dt;\r\n      }\r\n      if (torque) horn.to(cmdDeg, v); else { horn.limp(); cmdDeg = horn.angle; vel = 0; }\r\n      // what it reports\r\n      const pos = Math.round((horn.angle - (wheel ? 0 : base)) / DEG) + 2048;\r\n      set16(56, wheel ? ((pos % 4096) + 4096) % 4096 : Math.max(0, Math.min(4095, pos)));\r\n      const sp = Math.round(horn.speed / DEG);\r\n      set16(58, sp < 0 ? 0x8000 | Math.min(0x7fff, -sp) : Math.min(0x7fff, sp));\r\n      set16(60, horn.stalled ? 1000 : Math.min(1000, Math.round(Math.abs(cmdDeg - horn.angle) * 20)));\r\n      mem[62] = Math.round(v * 10);\r\n      mem[66] = Math.abs(goalDeg - horn.angle) > 1 || Math.abs(horn.speed) > 3 ? 1 : 0;\r\n      io.draw(torque ? (horn.stalled ? 2.7 : 0.18 + Math.abs(horn.speed) / 600) : 0.05);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (v < 4) return ['no power (6-8.4 V)'];\r\n      if (!baudOk) return ['messages at the wrong speed: it talks at 1,000,000 baud'];\r\n      return [`ID ${id()}, ${mem[33] === 1 ? `wheel mode, ${Math.round(sgn(w16(46)))} steps/s` : `to ${Math.round(goalDeg)} deg`}, at ${Math.round(horn.angle)} deg${mem[40] & 1 ? '' : ' (torque off)'}`, `${got} messages`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// Dynamixel XL430-W250 (Protocol 2.0): FF FF FD 00 id lenL lenH instr params crcL crcH, bytes\r\n// FF FF FD inside stuffed with an extra FD; at 57,600 baud. Control table (RAM): 64 torque enable,\r\n// 65 LED, 104 goal velocity (0.229 rpm), 112 profile velocity, 116 goal position, 122 moving,\r\n// 126 present load, 128 present velocity, 132 present position, 144 input voltage (0.1 V), 146\r\n// temperature; EEPROM: 0 model (1060), 7 ID, 8 baud (1 = 57,600), 11 operating mode (1 velocity,\r\n// 3 position, 4 extended position, 16 PWM). Torque is off at power-up.\r\nconst CRC_TABLE = (() => {\r\n  const t = [];\r\n  for (let i = 0; i < 256; i++) {\r\n    let c = i << 8;\r\n    for (let k = 0; k < 8; k++) c = c & 0x8000 ? ((c << 1) ^ 0x8005) & 0xffff : (c << 1) & 0xffff;\r\n    t.push(c);\r\n  }\r\n  return t;\r\n})();\r\nconst crc16 = (bytes) => {\r\n  let crc = 0;\r\n  for (const b of bytes) crc = ((crc << 8) ^ CRC_TABLE[((crc >> 8) ^ b) & 0xff]) & 0xffff;\r\n  return crc;\r\n};\r\nconst BAUDS = [9600, 57600, 115200, 1000000, 2000000, 3000000, 4000000, 4500000];\r\n\r\nbench.device('xl430', (part) => {\r\n  const horn = part.motor('horn');\r\n  const mem = new Array(160).fill(0);\r\n  mem[0] = 1060 & 255; mem[1] = 1060 >> 8; mem[6] = 46;\r\n  mem[7] = Number(part.params.id ?? 1) & 0xff;\r\n  mem[8] = 1; mem[11] = 3; mem[146] = 30;\r\n  mem[116] = 2048 & 255; mem[117] = 2048 >> 8; // (the goal starts where it is)\r\n  let rx = [], v = 0, goalDeg = 0, cmdDeg = 0, vel = 0, lastT = 0, got = 0, replies = [], baudOk = true, base = 0, lastMode = 3;\r\n  const id = () => mem[7];\r\n  const r32 = (a) => (mem[a] | (mem[a + 1] << 8) | (mem[a + 2] << 16) | (mem[a + 3] << 24));\r\n  const set32 = (a, x) => { for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) mem[a + i] = (x >> (8 * i)) & 255; };\r\n  const stuff = (b) => {\r\n    const out = [];\r\n    for (let i = 0; i < b.length; i++) {\r\n      out.push(b[i]);\r\n      if (i >= 2 && b[i - 2] === 0xff && b[i - 1] === 0xff && b[i] === 0xfd) out.push(0xfd);\r\n    }\r\n    return out;\r\n  };\r\n  const reply = (err, params = []) => {\r\n    const body = stuff([id(), 0, 0, 0x55, err, ...params]);\r\n    const len = body.length - 3 + 2; // instr .. crc\r\n    body[1] = len & 255; body[2] = len >> 8;\r\n    const pkt = [0xff, 0xff, 0xfd, 0x00, ...body];\r\n    const c = crc16(pkt);\r\n    replies.push([...pkt, c & 255, c >> 8]);\r\n  };\r\n  const goalFromMem = () => {\r\n    const raw = r32(116);\r\n    const mode = mem[11];\r\n    const pos = mode === 4 ? raw : Math.max(0, Math.min(4095, raw));\r\n    goalDeg = (mode === 4 ? 0 : base) + (pos - 2048) * DEG;\r\n  };\r\n  const handle = (tid, ins, params) => {\r\n    got++;\r\n    const forMe = tid === id() || tid === 0xfe;\r\n    if (!forMe) return;\r\n    if (ins === 0x01) { reply(0, [1060 & 255, 1060 >> 8, 46]); return; }\r\n    if (ins === 0x02 && tid === id()) {\r\n      const a = params[0] | (params[1] << 8), n = params[2] | (params[3] << 8);\r\n      reply(0, mem.slice(a, a + n));\r\n      return;\r\n    }\r\n    if (ins === 0x03 || ins === 0x04) {\r\n      const a = params[0] | (params[1] << 8), data = params.slice(2);\r\n      const torque = mem[64] & 1;\r\n      // (EEPROM: only with torque off; the mode, ID, baud live there)\r\n      if (a < 64 && torque) { if (tid === id()) reply(0x07); return; }\r\n      for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) if (a + i < 122) mem[a + i] = data[i]; // (from 122 on: read-only)\r\n      if (a <= 119 && a + data.length > 116) goalFromMem();\r\n      if (a <= 64 && a + data.length > 64 && (mem[64] & 1)) cmdDeg = horn.angle; // (torque on: it holds where it is)\r\n      if (tid === id()) reply(0);\r\n      return;\r\n    }\r\n    if (ins === 0x08) { mem[64] = 0; mem[11] = 3; mem[7] = 1; if (tid === id()) reply(0); return; } // factory reset\r\n  };\r\n  return {\r\n    packets(list) {\r\n      for (const p of list) {\r\n        if ((p.pin !== 'DATA' && p.pin !== 'DATA2') || p.proto !== 'uart') continue;\r\n        const baud = BAUDS[mem[8]] ?? 57600;\r\n        baudOk = !p.baud || Math.abs(p.baud - baud) < baud * 0.03;\r\n        if (!baudOk) continue;\r\n        rx.push(...p.data);\r\n      }\r\n      for (let guard = 0; guard < 64; guard++) { // (whole packets, a few at most)\r\n        const s = rx.findIndex((b, i) => b === 0xff && rx[i + 1] === 0xff && rx[i + 2] === 0xfd && rx[i + 3] === 0x00);\r\n        if (s < 0) { if (rx.length > 1024) rx = []; break; }\r\n        if (rx.length < s + 7) break;\r\n        const len = rx[s + 5] | (rx[s + 6] << 8);\r\n        if (rx.length < s + 7 + len) break;\r\n        const pkt = rx.slice(s, s + 7 + len);\r\n        rx = rx.slice(s + 7 + len);\r\n        const c = crc16(pkt.slice(0, -2));\r\n        if ((c & 255) !== pkt[pkt.length - 2] || (c >> 8) !== pkt[pkt.length - 1]) continue;\r\n        // unstuff the instruction's parameters\r\n        const raw = pkt.slice(8, -2), params = [];\r\n        for (let i = 0; i < raw.length; i++) {\r\n          params.push(raw[i]);\r\n          if (i >= 2 && raw[i - 2] === 0xff && raw[i - 1] === 0xff && raw[i] === 0xfd && raw[i + 1] === 0xfd) i++;\r\n        }\r\n        handle(pkt[4], pkt[7], params);\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      v = Math.max(supplied(io), io.supply('V+2', 'GND2'));\r\n      const dt = io.time - lastT;\r\n      lastT = io.time;\r\n      if (v < 5.5) { horn.limp(); rx = []; replies = []; io.draw(0); mem[64] = 0; return; }\r\n      for (const r of replies) io.send('DATA', 'uart', r, BAUDS[mem[8]] ?? 57600);\r\n      replies = [];\r\n      const torque = mem[64] & 1;\r\n      const mode = mem[11];\r\n      if (mode === 3 && lastMode !== 3) { base = 360 * Math.floor((horn.angle + 180) / 360); goalFromMem(); } // (position mode: one turn, the one it's in)\r\n      lastMode = mode;\r\n      const top = 57 * 6 * (v / 12);\r\n      const prof = r32(112);\r\n      const spd = prof > 0 ? Math.min(top, prof * 0.229 * 6) : top;\r\n      if (mode === 1) {\r\n        const want = Math.max(-top, Math.min(top, r32(104) * 0.229 * 6));\r\n        vel += Math.max(-2000 * dt, Math.min(2000 * dt, want - vel));\r\n        cmdDeg += vel * dt;\r\n      } else {\r\n        const d = goalDeg - cmdDeg;\r\n        const wantV = Math.sign(d) * Math.min(spd, Math.sqrt(2 * 3000 * Math.abs(d)));\r\n        vel += Math.max(-3000 * dt, Math.min(3000 * dt, wantV - vel));\r\n        if (Math.abs(d) < Math.abs(vel * dt) || Math.abs(d) < 0.05) { cmdDeg = goalDeg; vel = 0; } else cmdDeg += vel * dt;\r\n      }\r\n      if (torque) horn.to(cmdDeg, v); else { horn.limp(); cmdDeg = horn.angle; vel = 0; }\r\n      const pos = Math.round((horn.angle - (mode === 3 ? base : 0)) / DEG) + 2048;\r\n      set32(132, mode === 4 || mode === 1 ? pos : Math.max(0, Math.min(4095, pos)));\r\n      set32(128, Math.round(horn.speed / 6 / 0.229));\r\n      const load = horn.stalled ? 1000 : Math.min(1000, Math.round(Math.abs(cmdDeg - horn.angle) * 20));\r\n      mem[126] = load & 255; mem[127] = (load >> 8) & 255;\r\n      mem[144] = Math.round(v * 10) & 255; mem[145] = Math.round(v * 10) >> 8;\r\n      mem[122] = Math.abs(horn.speed) > 3 ? 1 : 0;\r\n      io.draw(torque ? (horn.stalled ? 1.4 : 0.06 + Math.abs(horn.speed) / 900) : 0.05);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (v < 5.5) return ['no power (6.5-12 V)'];\r\n      if (!baudOk) return [`messages at the wrong speed: it talks at ${BAUDS[mem[8]] ?? 57600} baud`];\r\n      const mode = { 1: 'velocity', 3: 'position', 4: 'extended position', 16: 'PWM' }[mem[11]] ?? `mode ${mem[11]}`;\r\n      return [`ID ${id()}, ${mode}, ${mem[64] & 1 ? (mem[11] === 1 ? `${Math.round(r32(104) * 0.229)} rpm` : `to ${Math.round(goalDeg)} deg`) : 'torque OFF (dxl.torqueOn(id))'}, at ${Math.round(horn.angle)} deg${mem[65] ? ', LED on' : ''}`, `${got} messages`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n","sketch":{"SCServo.h":{"classes":["SMS_STS","SCSCL"],"code":"// SCServo.h (Feetech's library) for STS servos (the STS3215):\n//   SMS_STS st;  Serial1.begin(1000000);  st.pSerial = &Serial1;\n//   st.WritePosEx(1, 2048, 2400, 50);   go to position 2048 (0-4095 = one turn) at 2400 steps/s, acceleration 50\n//   st.ReadPos(1), st.ReadSpeed(1), st.ReadLoad(1), st.ReadVoltage(1) (0.1 V), st.ReadTemper(1), st.ReadMove(1)\n//   st.WheelMode(1);  st.WriteSpe(1, 2000, 50);   spin as a wheel (steps/s, minus = backwards)\n//   st.EnableTorque(1, 0);  st.Ping(1);  st.FeedBack(1) then ReadPos(-1)...\n// Packets: FF FF id len instr params checksum; replies come back on the same wire.\nclass SMS_STS {\n  constructor(serial) {\n    this.pSerial = serial ?? null;\n    this.Error = 0;\n    this.IOTimeOut = 20; // ms\n    this.fb = null;\n  }\n  _port() {\n    if (!this.pSerial) throw new Error('SMS_STS: set its serial port first: st.pSerial = &Serial1;');\n    return this.pSerial;\n  }\n  _send(id, ins, params) {\n    const body = [id & 255, params.length + 2, ins, ...params.map((b) => b & 255)];\n    const chk = ~body.reduce((s, b) => s + b, 0) & 255;\n    const port = this._port();\n    while (port.available() > 0) port.read(); // (anything old)\n    port.write([0xff, 0xff, ...body, chk]);\n    port.flush();\n  }\n  /** a reply's parameters, or null (nobody answered in time / it was garbled) */\n  _reply(id) {\n    const port = this._port();\n    const buf = [];\n    const until = millis() + this.IOTimeOut;\n    for (;;) {\n      while (port.available() > 0) buf.push(port.read());\n      const s = buf.findIndex((b, i) => b === 0xff && buf[i + 1] === 0xff && buf[i + 2] === (id & 255));\n      if (s >= 0 && buf.length >= s + 4 && buf.length >= s + 4 + buf[s + 3]) {\n        const len = buf[s + 3];\n        const pkt = buf.slice(s + 2, s + 4 + len);\n        const chk = ~pkt.slice(0, -1).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) & 255;\n        if (chk !== pkt[pkt.length - 1]) return null;\n        this.Error = pkt[2];\n        return pkt.slice(3, -1);\n      }\n      if (millis() >= until) return null;\n      delay(1);\n    }\n  }\n  _write(id, addr, data) {\n    this._send(id, 0x03, [addr, ...data]);\n    if (id === 0xfe) return 1;\n    return this._reply(id) ? 1 : 0;\n  }\n  _read(id, addr, n) {\n    this._send(id, 0x02, [addr, n]);\n    return this._reply(id);\n  }\n  _word(x) { return [x & 255, (x >> 8) & 255]; }\n  _signed(x) { return x < 0 ? (-x & 0x7fff) | 0x8000 : x & 0x7fff; }\n  _unsigned(w) { return w & 0x8000 ? -(w & 0x7fff) : w; }\n  Ping(id) { this._send(id, 0x01, []); const r = this._reply(id); return r ? id : -1; }\n  writeByte(id, addr, v) { return this._write(id, addr, [v]); }\n  writeWord(id, addr, v) { return this._write(id, addr, this._word(v)); }\n  readByte(id, addr) { const r = this._read(id, addr, 1); return r ? r[0] : -1; }\n  readWord(id, addr) { const r = this._read(id, addr, 2); return r ? r[0] | (r[1] << 8) : -1; }\n  EnableTorque(id, en) { return this.writeByte(id, 40, en ? 1 : 0); }\n  unLockEprom(id) { return this.writeByte(id, 55, 0); }\n  LockEprom(id) { return this.writeByte(id, 55, 1); }\n  /** go to a position (0-4095 a turn) at a speed (steps/s, 0 = as fast as it can) and acceleration */\n  WritePosEx(id, pos, speed = 0, acc = 0) {\n    return this._write(id, 41, [acc, ...this._word(this._signed(pos)), 0, 0, ...this._word(speed)]);\n  }\n  RegWritePosEx(id, pos, speed = 0, acc = 0) { return this.WritePosEx(id, pos, speed, acc); }\n  RegWriteAction() { return 1; }\n  /** several at once: ids, how many, their positions, speeds, accelerations (arrays) */\n  SyncWritePosEx(ids, n, pos, speed, acc) {\n    const params = [41, 7];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) params.push(ids[i], acc ? acc[i] : 0, ...this._word(this._signed(pos[i])), 0, 0, ...this._word(speed ? speed[i] : 0));\n    this._send(0xfe, 0x83, params);\n  }\n  /** wheel mode: it spins (WriteSpe sets how fast) instead of going to positions */\n  WheelMode(id) { return this.writeByte(id, 33, 1); }\n  PosMode(id) { return this.writeByte(id, 33, 0); }\n  WriteSpe(id, speed, acc = 0) { return this._write(id, 41, [acc]) && this._write(id, 46, this._word(this._signed(speed))); }\n  /** read its state once; then ReadPos(-1) etc. give it without asking again */\n  FeedBack(id) { this.fb = this._read(id, 56, 15); return this.fb ? this.fb.length : -1; }\n  _fbWord(id, off, addr) {\n    if (id === -1) return this.fb ? this.fb[off] | (this.fb[off + 1] << 8) : -1;\n    const r = this._read(id, addr, 2);\n    return r ? r[0] | (r[1] << 8) : -1;\n  }\n  _fbByte(id, off, addr) {\n    if (id === -1) return this.fb ? this.fb[off] : -1;\n    const r = this._read(id, addr, 1);\n    return r ? r[0] : -1;\n  }\n  ReadPos(id) { const w = this._fbWord(id, 0, 56); return w < 0 ? -1 : this._unsigned(w); }\n  ReadSpeed(id) { const w = this._fbWord(id, 2, 58); return w < 0 ? -1 : this._unsigned(w); }\n  ReadLoad(id) { const w = this._fbWord(id, 4, 60); return w < 0 ? -1 : this._unsigned(w); }\n  ReadVoltage(id) { return this._fbByte(id, 6, 62); }\n  ReadTemper(id) { return this._fbByte(id, 7, 63); }\n  ReadMove(id) { return this._fbByte(id, 10, 66); }\n  ReadCurrent(id) { const l = this.ReadLoad(id); return l < 0 ? -1 : Math.round(Math.abs(l) * 2.5); }\n  ReadMode(id) { return this.readByte(id, 33); }\n  getErr() { return this.Error; }\n}\n// (the older SCS servos speak the same protocol)\nclass SCSCL extends SMS_STS {}\n"},"Dynamixel2Arduino.h":{"classes":["Dynamixel2Arduino"],"exports":["OP_POSITION","OP_EXTENDED_POSITION","OP_VELOCITY","OP_PWM","OP_CURRENT","OP_CURRENT_BASED_POSITION","UNIT_RAW","UNIT_PERCENT","UNIT_RPM","UNIT_DEGREE","UNIT_MILLI_AMPERE","TORQUE_ENABLE","LED","GOAL_POSITION","GOAL_VELOCITY","PROFILE_VELOCITY","PROFILE_ACCELERATION","PRESENT_POSITION","PRESENT_VELOCITY","PRESENT_LOAD","PRESENT_INPUT_VOLTAGE","PRESENT_TEMPERATURE","MOVING","OPERATING_MODE","ID","BAUD_RATE","MODEL_NUMBER"],"code":"// Dynamixel2Arduino.h (ROBOTIS), Protocol 2.0, for the XL430:\n//   Dynamixel2Arduino dxl(Serial1, DXL_DIR_PIN);   (the direction pin: -1 for none)\n//   dxl.begin(57600);  dxl.setPortProtocolVersion(2.0);  dxl.ping(1);\n//   dxl.torqueOff(1);  dxl.setOperatingMode(1, OP_POSITION);  dxl.torqueOn(1);\n//   dxl.setGoalPosition(1, 90.0, UNIT_DEGREE);  dxl.getPresentPosition(1, UNIT_DEGREE);\n//   dxl.setOperatingMode(1, OP_VELOCITY);  dxl.setGoalVelocity(1, 30, UNIT_RPM);\n//   dxl.ledOn(1);  dxl.readControlTableItem(PRESENT_INPUT_VOLTAGE, 1);  dxl.writeControlTableItem(PROFILE_VELOCITY, 1, 50);\nconst OP_VELOCITY = 1, OP_POSITION = 3, OP_EXTENDED_POSITION = 4, OP_CURRENT = 0, OP_CURRENT_BASED_POSITION = 5, OP_PWM = 16;\nconst UNIT_RAW = 0, UNIT_PERCENT = 1, UNIT_RPM = 2, UNIT_DEGREE = 3, UNIT_MILLI_AMPERE = 4;\n// control table items: [address, size] on the XL430\nconst MODEL_NUMBER = 1, ID = 2, BAUD_RATE = 3, OPERATING_MODE = 4, TORQUE_ENABLE = 5, LED = 6, GOAL_VELOCITY = 7, PROFILE_ACCELERATION = 8;\nconst PROFILE_VELOCITY = 9, GOAL_POSITION = 10, MOVING = 11, PRESENT_LOAD = 12, PRESENT_VELOCITY = 13, PRESENT_POSITION = 14;\nconst PRESENT_INPUT_VOLTAGE = 15, PRESENT_TEMPERATURE = 16;\nconst _DXL_ITEMS = {\n  1: [0, 2], 2: [7, 1], 3: [8, 1], 4: [11, 1], 5: [64, 1], 6: [65, 1], 7: [104, 4], 8: [108, 4], 9: [112, 4], 10: [116, 4],\n  11: [122, 1], 12: [126, 2], 13: [128, 4], 14: [132, 4], 15: [144, 2], 16: [146, 1],\n};\nconst _DXL_CRC = (() => {\n  const t = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < 256; i++) {\n    let c = i << 8;\n    for (let k = 0; k < 8; k++) c = c & 0x8000 ? ((c << 1) ^ 0x8005) & 0xffff : (c << 1) & 0xffff;\n    t.push(c);\n  }\n  return t;\n})();\nconst _dxlCrc = (bytes) => {\n  let crc = 0;\n  for (const b of bytes) crc = ((crc << 8) ^ _DXL_CRC[((crc >> 8) ^ b) & 0xff]) & 0xffff;\n  return crc;\n};\n\nclass Dynamixel2Arduino {\n  constructor(port, dirPin = -1) {\n    this.port = port; this.dir = dirPin; this.proto = 2.0; this.timeout = 30; this.lastErr = 0;\n  }\n  begin(baud = 57600) {\n    this.port.begin(baud);\n    if (this.dir >= 0) { pinMode(this.dir, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(this.dir, LOW); }\n    return true;\n  }\n  setPortProtocolVersion(v) { this.proto = v; return true; }\n  getPortProtocolVersion() { return this.proto; }\n  _send(id, ins, params) {\n    // byte stuffing: FF FF FD inside the parameters gets an extra FD\n    const stuffed = [];\n    const head = [0xff, 0xff, 0xfd, 0x00, id & 255, 0, 0, ins];\n    for (let i = 0; i < params.length; i++) {\n      stuffed.push(params[i] & 255);\n      const all = [...head, ...stuffed];\n      const n = all.length;\n      if (n >= 3 && all[n - 3] === 0xff && all[n - 2] === 0xff && all[n - 1] === 0xfd) stuffed.push(0xfd);\n    }\n    const len = stuffed.length + 3;\n    head[5] = len & 255; head[6] = len >> 8;\n    const pkt = [...head, ...stuffed];\n    const crc = _dxlCrc(pkt);\n    while (this.port.available() > 0) this.port.read();\n    if (this.dir >= 0) digitalWrite(this.dir, HIGH);\n    this.port.write([...pkt, crc & 255, crc >> 8]);\n    this.port.flush();\n    if (this.dir >= 0) digitalWrite(this.dir, LOW);\n  }\n  /** the status packet's parameters (after its error byte), or null */\n  _status(id) {\n    const buf = [];\n    const until = millis() + this.timeout;\n    for (;;) {\n      while (this.port.available() > 0) buf.push(this.port.read());\n      const s = buf.findIndex((b, i) => b === 0xff && buf[i + 1] === 0xff && buf[i + 2] === 0xfd && buf[i + 3] === 0x00 && buf[i + 4] === (id & 255));\n      if (s >= 0 && buf.length >= s + 7) {\n        const len = buf[s + 5] | (buf[s + 6] << 8);\n        if (buf.length >= s + 7 + len) {\n          const pkt = buf.slice(s, s + 7 + len);\n          const crc = _dxlCrc(pkt.slice(0, -2));\n          if ((crc & 255) !== pkt[pkt.length - 2] || (crc >> 8) !== pkt[pkt.length - 1]) return null;\n          this.lastErr = pkt[8];\n          const raw = pkt.slice(9, -2), out = [];\n          for (let i = 0; i < raw.length; i++) {\n            out.push(raw[i]);\n            if (i >= 2 && raw[i - 2] === 0xff && raw[i - 1] === 0xff && raw[i] === 0xfd && raw[i + 1] === 0xfd) i++;\n          }\n          return this.lastErr & 0x7f ? null : out;\n        }\n      }\n      if (millis() >= until) return null;\n      delay(1);\n    }\n  }\n  _write(id, addr, size, value) {\n    const data = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) data.push((value >> (8 * i)) & 255);\n    this._send(id, 0x03, [addr & 255, addr >> 8, ...data]);\n    return id === 0xfe ? true : this._status(id) !== null;\n  }\n  _read(id, addr, size) {\n    this._send(id, 0x02, [addr & 255, addr >> 8, size & 255, size >> 8]);\n    const r = this._status(id);\n    if (!r || r.length < size) return null;\n    let v = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) v |= r[i] << (8 * i);\n    if (size === 4) v |= 0; else if (size === 2 && v & 0x8000) v -= 0x10000;\n    return v;\n  }\n  ping(id) { this._send(id, 0x01, []); return this._status(id) !== null; }\n  getModelNumber(id) { return this._read(id, 0, 2) ?? 0; }\n  writeControlTableItem(item, id, value) { const [a, n] = _DXL_ITEMS[item] ?? [item, 1]; return this._write(id, a, n, Math.round(value)); }\n  readControlTableItem(item, id) { const [a, n] = _DXL_ITEMS[item] ?? [item, 1]; return this._read(id, a, n) ?? 0; }\n  torqueOn(id) { return this._write(id, 64, 1, 1); }\n  torqueOff(id) { return this._write(id, 64, 1, 0); }\n  getTorqueEnableStat(id) { return this._read(id, 64, 1) === 1; }\n  ledOn(id) { return this._write(id, 65, 1, 1); }\n  ledOff(id) { return this._write(id, 65, 1, 0); }\n  /** the mode can only change with the torque off (as the real one: this turns it off first) */\n  setOperatingMode(id, mode) { this.torqueOff(id); return this._write(id, 11, 1, mode); }\n  setID(id, newId) { this.torqueOff(id); return this._write(id, 7, 1, newId); }\n  setGoalPosition(id, value, unit = UNIT_RAW) {\n    const raw = unit === UNIT_DEGREE ? value / 0.088 : unit === UNIT_PERCENT ? (value / 100) * 4095 : value;\n    return this._write(id, 116, 4, Math.round(raw));\n  }\n  getPresentPosition(id, unit = UNIT_RAW) {\n    const r = this._read(id, 132, 4);\n    if (r === null) return 0;\n    return unit === UNIT_DEGREE ? r * 0.088 : unit === UNIT_PERCENT ? (r / 4095) * 100 : r;\n  }\n  setGoalVelocity(id, value, unit = UNIT_RAW) {\n    const raw = unit === UNIT_RPM ? value / 0.229 : unit === UNIT_PERCENT ? (value / 100) * 265 : value;\n    return this._write(id, 104, 4, Math.round(raw));\n  }\n  getPresentVelocity(id, unit = UNIT_RAW) {\n    const r = this._read(id, 128, 4);\n    if (r === null) return 0;\n    return unit === UNIT_RPM ? r * 0.229 : unit === UNIT_PERCENT ? (r / 265) * 100 : r;\n  }\n  getPresentCurrent(id) { const l = this._read(id, 126, 2); return l === null ? 0 : l * 2.69; }\n  getLastLibErrCode() { return this.lastErr; }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"fs90r","name":"Servo FS90R (continuous, micro)","description":"A micro servo that spins round and round: write(90) stops it, write(0) and write(180) are full speed each way, in between slower (no angle: it doesn't know where it is). 1.3 kg*cm, about 110 rpm at 4.8 V. Real ones stop a little off 90: the trim setting copies that.","swatch":"#1d1d20","mass":9,"shape":[{"box":[2.3,2.25,1.22],"at":[0,1.125,0],"color":"#1d1d20"},{"box":[3.5,0.22,1.22],"at":[0,1.665,0],"color":"#1d1d20"},{"cyl":[0.4026,0.35],"at":[0.55,2.425,0],"color":"#1d1d20"},{"box":[1.265,0.01,0.854],"at":[-0.345,1.125,0.616],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#2c5fd1","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"GND","label":"GND (brown)","at":[-1.75,0.45,-0.25],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+","label":"V+ (red)","at":[-1.75,0.45,0],"kind":"vin","vmin":4,"vmax":6.5},{"id":"SIG","label":"Signal (orange)","at":[-1.75,0.45,0.25],"kind":"in"}],"moving":[{"id":"horn","mass":1,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.5124,0.18],"at":[0.55,2.69,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[1.6,0.18,0.4392],"at":[1.35,2.69,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[0.3,0.02,0.12],"at":[0.855,2.79,0],"color":"#e33030","collide":false}],"joint":{"at":[0.55,2.6,0],"axis":[0,1,0],"motor":"motor","torque":1.3,"speed":110,"volts":4.8}}],"device":"cr-servo","params":[{"key":"trim","label":"Stop point trim (us)","kind":"number","min":-100,"max":100,"step":1}],"defaults":{"trim":0}},{"id":"mg996r-360","name":"Servo MG996R 360 (continuous)","description":"The metal-gear MG996R made to spin round and round: write(90) stops it, 0 and 180 are full speed each way (no angle: it doesn't know where it is). 10 kg*cm, about 55 rpm at 6 V: a good wheel motor.","swatch":"#202226","mass":55,"shape":[{"box":[4.07,3.78,1.97],"at":[0,1.89,0],"color":"#202226"},{"box":[5.2700000000000005,0.22,1.97],"at":[0,2.7971999999999997,0],"color":"#202226"},{"cyl":[0.6501,0.35],"at":[1,3.9549999999999996,0],"color":"#202226"},{"box":[2.2385,0.01,1.379],"at":[-0.6105,1.89,0.991],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#2c5fd1","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"GND","label":"GND (brown)","at":[-2.6350000000000002,0.45,-0.25],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+","label":"V+ (red)","at":[-2.6350000000000002,0.45,0],"kind":"vin","vmin":4,"vmax":7.4},{"id":"SIG","label":"Signal (orange)","at":[-2.6350000000000002,0.45,0.25],"kind":"in"}],"moving":[{"id":"horn","mass":3.3,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.8273999999999999,0.18],"at":[1,4.22,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[2.4,0.18,0.7091999999999999],"at":[2.2,4.22,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[0.3,0.02,0.12],"at":[1.4925,4.32,0],"color":"#e33030","collide":false}],"joint":{"at":[1,4.13,0],"axis":[0,1,0],"motor":"motor","torque":10,"speed":55,"volts":6}}],"device":"cr-servo","params":[{"key":"trim","label":"Stop point trim (us)","kind":"number","min":-100,"max":100,"step":1}],"defaults":{"trim":0}},{"id":"ds3218-270","name":"Servo DS3218 (270 deg)","description":"A 20 kg*cm digital servo with 270 degrees of travel: pulses 500-2500 us go from -135 to +135 deg. With Servo: write(0..180) covers the whole 270 (write(90) is the middle), or writeMicroseconds(). About 60 rpm at 6.8 V.","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":60,"shape":[{"box":[4,3.7,2],"at":[0,1.85,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"box":[5.45,0.22,2],"at":[0,2.738,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"cyl":[0.66,0.35],"at":[1,3.875,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"box":[2.2,0.01,1.4],"at":[-0.6,1.85,1.006],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#d03030","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"GND","label":"GND (brown)","at":[-2.6,0.45,-0.25],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+","label":"V+ (red)","at":[-2.6,0.45,0],"kind":"vin","vmin":4,"vmax":7.4},{"id":"SIG","label":"Signal (orange)","at":[-2.6,0.45,0.25],"kind":"in"}],"moving":[{"id":"horn","mass":3.5999999999999996,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.84,0.18],"at":[1,4.14,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[2.4,0.18,0.72],"at":[2.2,4.14,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[0.3,0.02,0.12],"at":[1.5,4.24,0],"color":"#e33030","collide":false}],"joint":{"at":[1,4.05,0],"axis":[0,1,0],"motor":"servo","torque":20,"speed":60,"volts":6.8,"min":-135,"max":135}}],"device":"pwm-servo","params":[{"key":"range","label":"Travel","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"270","label":"270 deg"}]}],"defaults":{"range":"270"}},{"id":"servo-360","name":"Servo 360 deg positional (25 kg)","description":"A positional servo with a full circle of travel: pulses 500-2500 us go from -180 to +180 deg (write(0..180) covers the whole circle, write(90) is the middle). It knows its angle, unlike a continuous servo. 25 kg*cm, about 50 rpm at 6.8 V.","swatch":"#24262b","mass":65,"shape":[{"box":[4,3.7,2],"at":[0,1.85,0],"color":"#24262b"},{"box":[5.45,0.22,2],"at":[0,2.738,0],"color":"#24262b"},{"cyl":[0.66,0.35],"at":[1,3.875,0],"color":"#24262b"},{"box":[2.2,0.01,1.4],"at":[-0.6,1.85,1.006],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#e0a020","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"GND","label":"GND (brown)","at":[-2.6,0.45,-0.25],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+","label":"V+ (red)","at":[-2.6,0.45,0],"kind":"vin","vmin":4,"vmax":7.4},{"id":"SIG","label":"Signal (orange)","at":[-2.6,0.45,0.25],"kind":"in"}],"moving":[{"id":"horn","mass":3.9,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.84,0.18],"at":[1,4.14,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[2.4,0.18,0.72],"at":[2.2,4.14,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[0.3,0.02,0.12],"at":[1.5,4.24,0],"color":"#e33030","collide":false}],"joint":{"at":[1,4.05,0],"axis":[0,1,0],"motor":"servo","torque":25,"speed":50,"volts":6.8,"min":-180,"max":180}}],"device":"pwm-servo","params":[{"key":"range","label":"Travel","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"360","label":"360 deg"}]}],"defaults":{"range":"360"}},{"id":"hs785hb","name":"Sail winch servo HS-785HB (3.5 turns)","description":"A multi-turn winch servo: pulses 600-2400 us go from -630 to +630 deg, three and a half turns end to end, and it holds there. writeMicroseconds(600..2400) (write(0..180) gives about two turns). 13 kg*cm, about 36 rpm at 6 V. Wind a line on its drum.","swatch":"#2a2a2e","mass":110,"shape":[{"box":[5.9,5,2.9],"at":[0,2.5,0],"color":"#2a2a2e"},{"box":[7.1000000000000005,0.22,2.9],"at":[0,3.7,0],"color":"#2a2a2e"},{"cyl":[0.957,0.35],"at":[1.6,5.175,0],"color":"#2a2a2e"},{"box":[3.2450000000000006,0.01,2.03],"at":[-0.885,2.5,1.456],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#3060c0","collide":false},{"cyl":[1.3,0.1],"at":[1.6,5.36,0],"color":"#c9cdd4","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"GND","label":"GND (brown)","at":[-3.5500000000000003,0.45,-0.25],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+","label":"V+ (red)","at":[-3.5500000000000003,0.45,0],"kind":"vin","vmin":4,"vmax":7.4},{"id":"SIG","label":"Signal (orange)","at":[-3.5500000000000003,0.45,0.25],"kind":"in"}],"moving":[{"id":"horn","mass":6.6,"shape":[{"cyl":[1.218,0.18],"at":[1.6,5.4399999999999995,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[1.2,0.18,1.044],"at":[2.2,5.4399999999999995,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[0.3,0.02,0.12],"at":[2.325,5.54,0],"color":"#e33030","collide":false}],"joint":{"at":[1.6,5.35,0],"axis":[0,1,0],"motor":"servo","torque":13.2,"speed":36,"volts":6,"multiturn":true}}],"device":"winch-servo"},{"id":"sts3215","name":"Smart servo Feetech STS3215","description":"A serial-bus smart servo: it knows its angle (0-4095 = one turn), and turns to a position or spins as a wheel; it reports where it is, its speed, load, voltage and temperature. 19.5 kg*cm, about 45 rpm at 7.4 V (6-8.4 V). Its DATA wire is one half-duplex serial line at 1,000,000 baud: wire both the board's TX and RX to it. Chain several on one bus (each its own ID). #include <SCServo.h>; SMS_STS st; Serial1.begin(1000000); st.pSerial = &Serial1; st.WritePosEx(1, 2048, 2000, 50);","swatch":"#141416","mass":55,"shape":[{"box":[4.52,3.15,2.47],"at":[0,1.575,0],"color":"#141416"},{"cyl":[0.8151000000000002,0.35],"at":[1.1,3.3249999999999997,0],"color":"#141416"},{"box":[2.4859999999999998,0.01,1.729],"at":[-0.6779999999999999,1.575,1.241],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#e0e0e0","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"GND","at":[-2.36,0.45,-0.85],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+","label":"V+ (6-8.4 V)","at":[-2.36,0.45,-0.6],"kind":"vin","vmin":4,"vmax":8.6},{"id":"DATA","label":"DATA (serial bus)","at":[-2.36,0.45,-0.35],"kind":"io"},{"id":"GND2","at":[-2.36,0.45,0.35],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+2","label":"V+ (6-8.4 V)","at":[-2.36,0.45,0.6],"kind":"vin","vmin":4,"vmax":8.6},{"id":"DATA2","label":"DATA (serial bus)","at":[-2.36,0.45,0.85],"kind":"io"}],"moving":[{"id":"horn","mass":3.3,"shape":[{"cyl":[1.0374,0.18],"at":[1.1,3.59,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[2,0.18,0.8892],"at":[2.1,3.59,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[0.3,0.02,0.12],"at":[1.7175000000000002,3.69,0],"color":"#e33030","collide":false}],"joint":{"at":[1.1,3.5,0],"axis":[0,1,0],"motor":"servo","torque":19.5,"speed":45,"volts":7.4,"multiturn":true}}],"device":"sts-servo","shorts":[["GND","GND2"],["V+","V+2"],["DATA","DATA2"]],"params":[{"key":"id","label":"Bus ID","kind":"number","min":0,"max":253,"step":1}],"defaults":{"id":1}},{"id":"xl430","name":"Smart servo Dynamixel XL430-W250","description":"ROBOTIS's smart servo (Protocol 2.0): position (one turn, or many in extended mode) or velocity, and it reports position, speed, load, voltage and temperature. Torque is off until you turn it on. 15 kg*cm (1.5 N*m), about 57 rpm at 12 V (6.5-12 V). DATA: one half-duplex serial line at 57,600 baud by default: wire both the board's TX and RX to it. #include <Dynamixel2Arduino.h>; Dynamixel2Arduino dxl(Serial1, -1); dxl.begin(57600); dxl.setPortProtocolVersion(2.0); dxl.torqueOn(1); dxl.setGoalPosition(1, 90.0, UNIT_DEGREE);","swatch":"#1d1d20","mass":57,"shape":[{"box":[4.65,2.87,2.85],"at":[0,1.435,0],"color":"#1d1d20"},{"cyl":[0.9405000000000001,0.35],"at":[1.2,3.045,0],"color":"#1d1d20"},{"box":[2.5575000000000006,0.01,1.9949999999999999],"at":[-0.6975,1.435,1.431],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#3a6fe0","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"GND","at":[-2.4250000000000003,0.45,-0.85],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+","label":"V+ (6.5-12 V, 11.1 V best)","at":[-2.4250000000000003,0.45,-0.6],"kind":"vin","vmin":5.5,"vmax":13},{"id":"DATA","label":"DATA (serial bus)","at":[-2.4250000000000003,0.45,-0.35],"kind":"io"},{"id":"GND2","at":[-2.4250000000000003,0.45,0.35],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"V+2","label":"V+ (6.5-12 V, 11.1 V best)","at":[-2.4250000000000003,0.45,0.6],"kind":"vin","vmin":5.5,"vmax":13},{"id":"DATA2","label":"DATA (serial bus)","at":[-2.4250000000000003,0.45,0.85],"kind":"io"}],"moving":[{"id":"horn","mass":3.42,"shape":[{"cyl":[1.197,0.18],"at":[1.2,3.31,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[1.8,0.18,1.026],"at":[2.1,3.31,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[0.3,0.02,0.12],"at":[1.9125,3.41,0],"color":"#e33030","collide":false}],"joint":{"at":[1.2,3.22,0],"axis":[0,1,0],"motor":"servo","torque":15.3,"speed":57,"volts":12,"multiturn":true}}],"device":"xl430","shorts":[["GND","GND2"],["V+","V+2"],["DATA","DATA2"]],"params":[{"key":"id","label":"Bus ID","kind":"number","min":0,"max":253,"step":1}],"defaults":{"id":1}}],"examples":[{"name":"Continuous servos and a knob","description":"An FS90R and an MG996R 360 on one knob (its slider in the run panel): the middle stops them, either side spins them that way, faster the further you go. write() sets speed, not an angle.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Continuous servos and a knob","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-12,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"knob","type":"knob","name":"Speed knob","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[-12,0,9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"small","type":"servos/fs90r","name":"FS90R (continuous)","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[2,0,-5],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"big","type":"servos/mg996r-360","name":"MG996R 360 (continuous)","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,6],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"batt","type":"battery-4aa","name":"Servo batteries","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[-2,0,14],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"L"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"H"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"A0"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"W"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"small","pin":"V+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"small","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"small","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"big","pin":"V+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"big","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"big","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#f08a24"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Continuous servos: turn the knob (its slider in the run panel). The middle stops both servos; to\n// either side they spin that way, faster the further you go. write() sets SPEED, not an angle.\n#include <Servo.h>\n\n#define KNOB A0\nServo small;    // FS90R\nServo big;      // MG996R 360\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  small.attach(2);\n  big.attach(3);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int speed = map(analogRead(KNOB), 0, 4095, 0, 180);   // 90 = stop\n  small.write(speed);\n  big.write(speed);\n  Serial.print(\"write(\");\n  Serial.print(speed);\n  if (speed == 90) Serial.println(\") = stop\");\n  else if (speed < 90) Serial.println(\") = one way\");\n  else Serial.println(\") = the other way\");\n  delay(200);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"270, 360 and winch","description":"A 270 deg servo, a 360 deg servo and a sail winch servo side by side, all swept by one knob (their run-panel slider): see how far each one turns for the same signal.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"270, 360 and winch","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-14,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"knob","type":"knob","name":"Knob","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[-14,0,9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"s270","type":"servos/ds3218-270","name":"270 deg servo","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,-7],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"s360","type":"servos/servo-360","name":"360 deg servo","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,2],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"winch","type":"servos/hs785hb","name":"Winch servo","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[2,0,11],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"batt","type":"battery-4aa","name":"Servo batteries","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[-8,0,16],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"L"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"H"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"A0"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"W"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"s270","pin":"V+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"s270","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"s270","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"s360","pin":"V+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"s360","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"s360","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#f08a24"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"winch","pin":"V+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"winch","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP4"},"b":{"uid":"winch","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w13","a":{"uid":"batt","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// 270, 360 and a winch: one knob (its slider in the run panel) moves all three. The same signal\n// turns each one a different amount: 270 deg, a full circle, three and a half turns.\n#include <Servo.h>\n\n#define KNOB A0\nServo s270;\nServo s360;\nServo winch;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  s270.attach(2);\n  s360.attach(3);\n  winch.attach(4);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int k = analogRead(KNOB);                   // 0 .. 4095\n  int angle = map(k, 0, 4095, 0, 180);        // write(0..180): each servo's whole range\n  s270.write(angle);\n  s360.write(angle);\n  int us = map(k, 0, 4095, 600, 2400);        // the winch's range is 600 .. 2400 us\n  winch.writeMicroseconds(us);\n  Serial.print(\"270 servo: \");\n  Serial.print(map(angle, 0, 180, -135, 135));\n  Serial.print(\" deg   360 servo: \");\n  Serial.print(map(angle, 0, 180, -180, 180));\n  Serial.print(\" deg   winch: \");\n  Serial.print(map(us, 600, 2400, -630, 630));\n  Serial.println(\" deg\");\n  delay(250);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Smart servos","description":"An STS3215 (on Serial1) and a Dynamixel XL430 (on Serial2), each on its own battery: the board turns them to angles, spins the STS as a wheel, and prints where they say they are.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Smart servos","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-14,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"sts","type":"servos/sts3215","name":"STS3215","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[2,0,-6],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"xl","type":"servos/xl430","name":"XL430","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[2,0,7],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"b74","type":"battery-18650","name":"7.4 V for the STS","params":{"count":"2","charge":100},"parent":null,"pos":[-6,0,-14],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"b11","type":"battery-lipo","name":"11.1 V for the XL430","params":{"cells":"3","mAh":1500,"charge":100},"parent":null,"pos":[-6,0,15],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"b74","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"sts","pin":"V+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"b74","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"sts","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP0"},"b":{"uid":"sts","pin":"DATA"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP1"},"b":{"uid":"sts","pin":"DATA"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"b11","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"xl","pin":"V+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"b11","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"xl","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP4"},"b":{"uid":"xl","pin":"DATA"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP5"},"b":{"uid":"xl","pin":"DATA"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"b74","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"b11","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Smart servos: an STS3215 on Serial1 (1,000,000 baud) and a Dynamixel XL430 on Serial2 (57,600).\n// They turn to angles, the STS spins as a wheel for a while, and both say where they are.\n#include <SCServo.h>\n#include <Dynamixel2Arduino.h>\n\nSMS_STS st;\nDynamixel2Arduino dxl(Serial2, -1);\nconst int STS_ID = 1;\nconst int DXL_ID = 1;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  Serial1.begin(1000000);\n  st.pSerial = &Serial1;\n  dxl.begin(57600);\n  dxl.setPortProtocolVersion(2.0);\n  Serial.print(\"STS3215: \");\n  if (st.Ping(STS_ID) == STS_ID) Serial.println(\"answered\");\n  else Serial.println(\"no answer: check its wires and battery\");\n  Serial.print(\"XL430: \");\n  if (dxl.ping(DXL_ID)) Serial.println(\"answered\");\n  else Serial.println(\"no answer: check its wires and battery\");\n  dxl.torqueOff(DXL_ID);\n  dxl.setOperatingMode(DXL_ID, OP_POSITION);\n  dxl.torqueOn(DXL_ID);\n}\n\nvoid report() {\n  Serial.print(\"STS at \");\n  Serial.print(st.ReadPos(STS_ID));\n  Serial.print(\" (of 4096), \");\n  Serial.print(st.ReadVoltage(STS_ID) / 10.0, 1);\n  Serial.print(\" V   XL430 at \");\n  Serial.print(dxl.getPresentPosition(DXL_ID, UNIT_DEGREE), 1);\n  Serial.println(\" deg\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  st.WritePosEx(STS_ID, 1024, 2400, 50);      // a quarter turn one way\n  dxl.setGoalPosition(DXL_ID, 90.0, UNIT_DEGREE);\n  delay(1500);\n  report();\n  st.WritePosEx(STS_ID, 3072, 2400, 50);      // a quarter turn the other way\n  dxl.setGoalPosition(DXL_ID, 270.0, UNIT_DEGREE);\n  delay(1500);\n  report();\n  st.WheelMode(STS_ID);                       // now spin as a wheel for two seconds\n  st.WriteSpe(STS_ID, 2000, 50);\n  delay(2000);\n  st.WriteSpe(STS_ID, 0, 50);\n  delay(300);\n  st.PosMode(STS_ID);\n  report();\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}